success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Caveat:** I can't confirm the 2026 amendment text is final, and the regulation and Q&A numbering may be misremembered. Check the current consolidated Central Bank UCITS Regulations and Q&A before relying on this.\n\n**Express 2026 approach (Reg. 26(2), as amended):**\n- **Cash vs in-kind:** Cash dealing may have an earlier cut-off than in-kind, giving time to trade underlying securities.\n- **Hedged vs unhedged:** Currency-hedged classes may have an earlier cut-off than unhedged ones, allowing FX hedge execution.\n- **Conditions:** Cut-offs must be disclosed in the prospectus, objectively justified, and precede the valuation point. No forward-pricing breach or late trading.\n\n**Older Q&A 1030 approach:**\n- Equal treatment required one dealing deadline for all classes.\n- Different deadlines needed a case-by-case Central Bank derogation on operational grounds.\n- Permission came via prospectus review, not an express regulatory right.","ttft_ms":1629,"type":"result","duration_ms":3718,"uuid":"5d487135-a52f-4ae3-b90a-1ccbc116b4ac","ttft_stream_ms":1150,"time_to_request_ms":55,"first_content_frame_ms":1150,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
